In contest 1, if $L_1 \le X \le R_1$, rating becomes $X+1$. Else $X$.
In contest 2, if $L_2 \le \text{current\_rating} \le R_2$, rating increases.
And so on.

Since the rating only increases, the condition $L_i \le \text{current\_rating} \le R_i$ depends on the current rating.
However, notice that the rating increases by at most 1 in each contest.
Specifically, if the rating starts at $X$, after contest $i$, the rating is $X + k_i$, where $k_i$ is the number of times the condition was met in contests $1$ through $i$.
